      "evidence_quote": "The payment spreadsheet labels it 'donation', and Robyn wrote in a message that she wanted to help the animals.",
      "id": "a1",
      "justification": "The scenario explicitly states that the payment is labeled as a 'donation' in the spreadsheet and Robyn described it as helping animals, which supports the proposition that it is a donation.",
      "status": "TRUE"
    },
    {
      "evidence_quote": "The coordinator's booking sheet shows the placements as 'awaiting settlement' until 4 February, when the £260 arrived; the same sheet then changed to 'confirmed'. The March newsletter archive and the dated website capture show the link in the agreed locations. A later volunteer note says 'we didn't raise an invoice, so I called it a donation'.",
      "id": "a2",
      "justification": "The absence of an invoice and the description of the payment as a donation in a volunteer note, combined with the fact that it was not tied to a purchase or service, supports that it is not a payment for goods or services or made because the charity bought goods and services.",
      "status": "TRUE"
    },
    {
      "evidence_quote": "The payment spreadsheet labels it 'donation', and Robyn wrote in a message that she wanted to help the animals. Robyn runs a local grooming salon, and the arrangement was for promotional placements on the newsletter and website.",
      "id": "a3",
      "justification": "There is no evidence that the £260 was made through Payroll Giving. The payment originated from a personal donation arrangement, not a payroll arrangement, so it is not a Payroll Giving payment.",
      "status": "TRUE"
    },
    {
      "evidence_quote": "A later volunteer note says 'we didn't raise an invoice, so I called it a donation'.",
      "id": "a4",
      "justification": "The volunteer note indicates that the payment was not made for a benefit over a certain limit, as no invoice was raised and the transaction was described as a donation, which implies it was not a benefit-based payment.",
      "status": "TRUE"
    },
    {
      "evidence_quote": "The donation of £260 from Robyn Ellis on 4 February 2026 is not a payment of shares.",
      "id": "a5",
      "justification": "There is no mention of shares or any form of equity being transferred. The transaction is described as a donation to help animals, not a share payment.",
      "status": "TRUE"
    },
    {
      "evidence_quote": "A later volunteer note says 'we didn't raise an invoice, so I called it a donation'.",
      "id": "a6",
      "justification": "There is no reference to charity cards or vouchers such as CAF vouchers. The payment is described as a personal donation, not originating from a voucher or card.",
      "status": "TRUE"
    },
    {
      "evidence_quote": "We have the charity's HMRC recognition letter.",
      "id": "a7",
      "justification": "The HMRC recognition letter confirms that the charity is recognized for tax purposes, which satisfies the requirement under E02.",
      "status": "TRUE"
    },
    {
      "evidence_quote": "Robyn's personal tax position and whether she completed a Gift Aid form for the £260 have not been checked.",
      "id": "a8",
      "justification": "There is no evidence about Robyn's tax position or how much she paid in Income Tax or Capital Gains Tax. The absence of verification means the proposition is not established as true or false.",
